# MESSAGE: known-implies-no-LLM violation -- a ashdspy:CompiledRoute
# selecting an ashdspy:LLMImplementation while a NON-LLM implementation
# (lattice rungs 1..7) exists for the SAME Signature with a PASSING
# ashdspy:CourtVerdict is a violation row naming the route. This is the
# KNOWN => Allocation_LLM = 0 law as a refusal: intelligence is demoted to
# residue the moment a lower rung is witnessed. An LLM route with NO
# passing lower-rung alternative is lawful (that is the UNKNOWN residue --
# LLM keeps only what nothing lower can hold).
# Violation-row style (FM-PACK-013): zero rows = the lattice allocation is
# lawful; one row per LLM route that outranks a proven lower rung.
# Join law: the route's signature (?sig) and LLM implementation (?llm) are
# the outer BGP; the qualifying alternative is a POSITIVE existence
# condition, so it is matched via OPTIONAL + group-level FILTER(BOUND)
# (the negated-existence crash law never engages: no EXISTS anywhere).
# VALUES carries the 7 non-LLM lattice classes (locked-engines-proven
# below; the UNION fallback was not needed). The alternative must be bound
# to the same ?sig via ashdspy:forSignature AND hold a courtVerdict with
# ashdspy:passed true.
PREFIX ashdspy: <https://seanchatmangpt.github.io/packs/ashdspy#>
SELECT ?route ?sig ?llm ?knownAlt WHERE {
  ?route a ashdspy:CompiledRoute ;
         ashdspy:compiles ?sig ;
         ashdspy:routeImplementation ?llm .
  ?llm a ashdspy:LLMImplementation .
  OPTIONAL {
    VALUES ?t { ashdspy:ReuseImplementation ashdspy:ComposeImplementation
                ashdspy:RuleImplementation ashdspy:PlanImplementation
                ashdspy:ConstraintImplementation ashdspy:GenerateImplementation
                ashdspy:SpecializedModelImplementation }
    ?knownAlt a ?t ;
              ashdspy:forSignature ?sig ;
              ashdspy:courtVerdict ?altVerdict .
    ?altVerdict ashdspy:passed true .
  }
  FILTER(BOUND(?knownAlt))
}
ORDER BY ?route ?knownAlt
